  "summary": "Interpreting gradient boosted trees as the supplied Boosted Decision-Tree Ensembles method, four candidates directly apply that method to mapping active wildfire extent. [V0184] is strongest on a higher-is-better metric, reporting Atlas-ICU test F1=0.93; [V0183] reports MetroFlow AUROC=0.86. [V0181] evaluates on FireScope with accuracy=0.72, whereas [V0182] reports ChurnBench MAE=0.79; because MAE is an error metric and datasets differ, [V0182] is not treated as directly comparable to the F1/AUROC/accuracy reports. No fifth supplied candidate satisfies both the requested method and requested topic: [V0185] concerns mapping active wildfire extent but uses multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling, so it is not evidence for gradient-boosted-tree wildfire mapping.",
